{"type": "result", "session_id": "20260930_155101_aff521", "exit_code": 0, "text": "**Email 1: Subject: Managing Total Cost When Cloud and Laptops Overlap**\n\nMorgan,\n\nWhen engineers need both cloud workstations for CAD and laptops for site work, the monthly cloud bill often grows beyond expectations. Many firms find they're paying for both cloud resources and powerful local hardware, without a clear view of total fleet cost.\n\nAurora is different. It's a 14-inch mobile workstation designed for engineers who run AI models locally while maintaining client data under your firm's control. At 1.65 kg, it works on-site where connectivity fails. With Windows 11 Pro, TPM 2.0, and a 3-year on-site warranty, it reduces device count and service complexity.\n\nIf you're looking to understand the real cost of your hybrid setup, let's discuss. Would you be open to a 15-minute conversation about total fleet cost?\n\nBest,\n[Your Name]\n\n---\n\n**Email 2: Subject: Why Cloud-First Teams Still Need Local AI Workstations**\n\nMorgan,\n\nI understand your concern: \"We already pay for cloud workstations. Why buy powerful laptops too?\"\n\nCloud is ideal for CAD. But engineers increasingly want to run AI tools directly on client drawings. The Aurora 14 AI Workstation runs open-weight language models up to 30 billion parameters locally\u2014no cloud dependency. It has a Helix H9 AI processor with 60 TOPS NPU and 32 GB standard memory (upgradable to 128 GB).\n\nWhen connectivity fails on-site, your engineers can still work. The 14-inch OLED display (500 nits, 120 Hz) handles technical drawings clearly. With Thunderbolt 5 ports and an SD card reader, file transfers remain efficient.\n\nWould you like to see how this fits your current fleet strategy?\n\nBest,\n[Your Name]\n\n---\n\n**Email 3: Subject: Q1 Budget Planning for AI-Ready Engineering Hardware**\n\nMorgan,\n\nYour budget cycle closes at the end of Q1. Anything not approved waits a year.\n\nThe Aurora 14 AI Workstation ships in Q4 at $2,899 (base configuration). That means you can approve it now and receive it when your budget opens. With 32 GB memory, up to 128 GB expandable, and a 3-year on-site warranty, it's built for long-term use.\n\nSecurity matters. It includes fingerprint reader, IR camera, TPM 2.0, and self-healing BIOS. Client data stays under your control.\n\nCan we schedule a meeting to discuss how this aligns with your Q1 planning?\n\nBest,\n[Your Name]", "tokens": {"input": 847, "output": 573, "total": 5239, "cache_read": 3819, "cache_write": 0}, "duration_ms": 67303, "timestamp": 1790808728779}